course: dictionary
lesson: 6824
title: The word otherwise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Otherwise is a small word that points to a choice. It tells you what happens if something is not done, or what is true in the other case. «Hold the rail, otherwise you might fall.» The word otherwise warns you: if you do not hold the rail, you might fall.
explain: Look at the words around otherwise to find its meaning. «If it is even, put it in box A; otherwise, put it in box B.» Every number that is not even goes in box B, so otherwise means "in the other case".
explain: Otherwise can also mean "apart from that" or "in a different way". «Boredom makes you notice things you would otherwise miss.» Here it means "if this were not the case". When you meet otherwise, ask: what is the other case, or what would happen instead? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: Otherwise means "if not" or "or else": what will happen if something is not done.
fact: Otherwise can also mean "apart from that" or "in other ways".
fact: Otherwise can mean "differently", as in «unless told otherwise».
fact: Phrases with otherwise include «or otherwise» and «think otherwise».
fact: Otherwise is an adverb, and it also works as a joining word that means "or else".
exercise: «Wear your coat, otherwise you will be cold.» What does otherwise mean here? | *If you do not, you will be cold | Very quietly | Apart from that, you are fine | In a different way
exercise: «If the number is odd, put it in box X; otherwise, put it in box Y.» Where does an even number go? | Under the table | Box X | *Box Y | Neither box
exercise: «Money must go to that cause unless everyone agreed otherwise.» What does otherwise mean here? | *In a different way | Very quickly | Loudly | Always
test: «People looking at phones while crossing miss cars they would otherwise have seen.» What does otherwise mean here? | Slowly, one step at a time | *If they were not looking at phones | In a loud way | Very carefully
test: «I used to like rain, but now I think otherwise.» What does think otherwise mean? | I am lost in thought | I am sure the rain is great | I am cold and wet | *I have changed my mind
exam: «Use the swap test; otherwise, it is their, your or its.» What does otherwise mean in this sentence? | Apart from that | In a loud way | Very quickly | *In any other case, if the swap does not fit
